() Tj T*
(Issuer metadata for ministerial decisions is parsed from PDF URLs like) Tj T*
(data.qanoon.om/ar/md/{issuer}/2026-0074.pdf. This is more reliable than asking an LLM to) Tj T*
(infer the issuer from prose.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cross-reference edges are extracted from inline qanoon.om links and local Arabic legal) Tj T*
(keywords. ??? ??????? ??? maps to REFERENCES; ???? maps to REPEALS; and ????, ????, ??????,) Tj T*
(and ???? map to AMENDS. This gives exact, auditable graph edges without topic-model) Tj T*
(hallucination.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( LLM, Embeddings, And Retrieval) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The LLM is constrained to topic extraction and optional final answer synthesis. Google) Tj T*
(Gemini is supported directly through the Generative Language REST API. Topic extraction) Tj T*
(receives a seed taxonomy and returns JSON. If no API key is configured, a deterministic) Tj T*
(keyword fallback keeps the pipeline runnable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The default embedding model is intfloat/multilingual-e5-small, chosen because Arabic) Tj T*
(coverage matters more here than marginal English-only gains. Chunks are formed around) Tj T*
(Markdown headings and then windowed to roughly 500-900 tokens with overlap.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The search client implements three retrieval stages in both local and Neo4j-backed modes:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Candidate generation with dense vector scores and sparse keyword/full-text scores. The) Tj T*
(default dense weight is 0.35 because the current legal sanity checks showed exact sparse) Tj T*
(matches are more reliable for title-heavy ministerial decisions than uncalibrated dense) Tj T*
(scores.) Tj T*
(2. Graph expansion by appending parent document metadata, linked topics, and legal) Tj T*
(references. In Neo4j mode this expansion is performed with live Cypher traversals from) Tj T*
(retrieved Chunk nodes to their parent Document, Topic, and legal-reference relationships.) Tj T*
(3. Optional cross-encoder reranking with BAAI/bge-reranker-base.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Final synthesis uses Gemini when GOOGLE_API_KEY is configured, with an OpenAI-compatible) Tj T*
(fallback also available. Without an LLM key, the client returns an extractive answer with) Tj T*
(source titles and snippets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Bonus Features And Limits) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Topic merging is implemented as a vector-similarity audit with a default threshold of 0.88.) Tj T*
(The threshold is intentionally conservative: it catches close synonyms while reducing the) Tj T*
(risk of merging adjacent but legally distinct concepts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Community detection is included as exploratory analysis via Louvain over the document-topic-) Tj T*
(reference graph. Each community can be summarized by the configured LLM using its topic) Tj T*
(labels and representative document titles. It is not treated as the main quality claim) Tj T*
(because sparse legal citation graphs can cluster by issuer, time, or publication pattern) Tj T*
(instead of substantive legal field.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cross-encoder reranking is optional. It can improve precision, but it is slower than bi-) Tj T*
(encoder retrieval. The intended production optimization path would be async candidate) Tj T*
(generation, cached graph expansion, batched reranker inference, and quantized reranker) Tj T*
(weights.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Retrieval Evaluation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The six-document sample is only a smoke test. To avoid overstating quality, a separate) Tj T*
(evaluation harness runs labeled known-answer queries and reports Hit@1, Hit@3, and Mean) Tj T*
(Reciprocal Rank. A broader local run inspected 80 live Qanoon posts and produced 67 full) Tj T*
ET
endstream
